ref 17592186045417] [17592186125269 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125270 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125270 #edb/ref 1061 10559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125270 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4f4f64aa-ab4f-5abb-8d9c-ca2aa2790b64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125270 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125271 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125271 #edb/ref 1061 10563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125271 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a25341f7-8d06-561b-9802-42d2f9c792e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125271 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125272 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125272 #edb/ref 1061 10566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125272 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f8b4cf47-e81c-516c-8eef-7d544743362a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125272 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125273 #edb/ref 1061 10567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125273 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "25a77626-7a96-5d1b-b087-a01012cbeb91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125273 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125724 #edb/ref 1064 "Just like we can compute second derivatives of single-variable functions, we can also compute second derivatives of multivariable functions.\n\nFor example, consider the two-variable function\n\n$$\nf (x, y)= x y^2 + e^{xy}.\n$$\n\nIts two first-order partial derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & ={y}^{2}+y{e}^{xy}, \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =2xy+x{e}^{xy}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f_x(x,y)$ and $f_y(x,y)$ are themselves functions that are differentiable with respect to both $x$ and $y,$ we can compute the **second-order partial derivatives** as well. \n\n- The partial derivatives of $f_x(x,y)$ with respect to $x$ and $y,$ denoted $f_{xx}$ and $f_{xy}$ respectively, are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{x}(x,y))={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}, \\\\ {f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y))=2y+xy{e}^{xy}+{e}^{xy}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The partial derivatives of $f_y(x,y)$ with respect to $x$ and $y,$ denoted $f_{yx}$ and $f_{yy}$ respectively, are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y))=2y+xy{e}^{xy}+{e}^{xy}, \\\\ {f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{y}(x,y))=2x+{x}^{2}{e}^{xy}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe partial derivatives $f_{xy}$ and $f_{yx}$ are called **mixed partial derivatives** because they involve taking the partial derivatives with respect to different variables, $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe following alternative notations are also widely used to represent second-order partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂{x}^{2}}(f) & =\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}={f}_{xx}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂{y}^{2}}(f)=\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}={f}_{yy} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂y\\,∂x}(f) & =\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y\\,∂x}={f}_{xy}\\,\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂x\\,∂y}(f)=\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x\\,∂y}={f}_{yx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In our example, the two mixed partial derivatives were equal:\n\n$$\nf_{xy}(x,y) = 2y + xye^{xy} + e^{xy} = f_{yx}(x,y)\n$$\n\nLater, we will see that under rather mild conditions on $f,$ we almost always have that $f_{xy}=f_{yx}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125724 #edb/ref 1065 2397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125724 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "feb54aa0-17fb-5468-8b99-14174a6bd059" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125724 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125725 #edb/ref 1064 "We can also define other **higher order partial derivatives** such as $f_{xxy}, \\, f_{xxyy}, \\, f_{xyxy},$ etc. \n\nFor instance, the function $f(x,y,z)= z\\cos(xy)$ has the first-order partial derivative\n\n$$\nf_y(x,y,z) = -xz \\sin(xy)\n$$\n\nand the second-order partial derivative\n\n$$\nf_{yx}(x,y,z)= -x yz \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} - z\\sin{\\left(x y \\right)}.\n$$\n\nIf we differentiate again, with respect to $x,$ then we get the **third-order partial derivative** $f_{yxx}\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{yx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-xyz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =-yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xyz(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y)-z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\cdot y \\\\  & =x{y}^{2}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, to compute a $n$th-order partial derivative, we need to compute a sequence of $n$ individual derivatives." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125725 #edb/ref 1065 2398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125725 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e256986d-ca95-50b3-a16c-0f46005b5c66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125725 #edb/ref 1067 "Higher-Order Partial Derivatives for Functions of  More Than Two Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266152 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266152 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266152 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "00508df2-67fc-5789-9478-c3e2d42771e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266758 #edb/ref 1080 "-2\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266758 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266758 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "44da4fc7-1df8-536a-a190-f8c23a3e32f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266921 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{3}-\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266921 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266921 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "573ca17f-8b55-50aa-b136-59bd043a6536" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266974 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266974 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266974 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5df633bf-d9fe-5623-9aed-bd0cc78f2d1c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266989 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}+\\pi )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266989 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266989 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5fc7ddd0-7d66-560f-b925-d71f0a4f1da7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267021 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267021 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267021 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "63a9b984-28e7-58d3-8128-0a6d4ca98f26" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267184 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -\\sqrt{3})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267184 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267184 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "75e2d132-79e6-565d-b0a0-3480a84f1042" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267363 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267363 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267363 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "88f1885b-f866-5cf3-96ea-874e43e6a210" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267416 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267416 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267416 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8ebfbd8f-e225-52f2-af81-73501dcd099d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267685 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267685 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267685 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aa6cc2bf-6cc9-5989-82ab-f94ca56c41d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268418 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268418 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268418 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268418 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268418 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268418 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268418 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268418 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186266974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268418 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0722938f-1bbb-5341-b742-6808aa83c68d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268545 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268545 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268545 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268545 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268545 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268545 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268545 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268545 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186266152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268545 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4f17d030-5507-55e9-8f15-4689404588ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268920 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268920 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132894" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268920 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268920 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)-{g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ given that ${g}_{x}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)$ and ${g}_{y}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268920 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3aaf83dc-c135-54d5-b395-8dc2f637ad0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268920 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we evaluate ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ and ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\ {g}_{yy}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{xx}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})-{g}_{yy}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268923 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268923 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132961" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268923 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268923 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${f}_{xxz}(1,\\frac{1}{2},\\pi )$ for $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268923 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "01b2f238-4be0-502a-a439-500d85cd72b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268923 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡xyz) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\cdot yz \\\\  & =yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{xx}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{x}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =yz\\cdot (-yz\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xxz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xx}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xxz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({f}_{xx}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\cdot (2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)+xy{z}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}z(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)+xyz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{xxz}(x,y,z)$ at $(1,\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xxz}(1,\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ) & =-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi )+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333031 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{4y}{{x}^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333031 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333031 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0548138d-e543-5a54-a872-c6505ae35f31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333573 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2y}{x}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333573 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333573 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3dd21545-2656-5f34-8899-9e63ce0f1a99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333777 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333777 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186333777 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56f12986-c08d-5855-9c32-e38ca3128af3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334026 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{y}{4x}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334026 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334026 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7279d9a1-e1cd-5962-b045-74040fa8edd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334135 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{4+y}{x}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334135 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186334135 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "810185ca-f52f-5e5b-a85b-df54ad11e6a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335605 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186333031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335605 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186333573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335605 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186333777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335605 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186334026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335605 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186334135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335605 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335605 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335605 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186333031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335605 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c7a6c17f-ff74-5dd2-941a-c73839c7e4a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335788 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186335605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335788 #edb/ref 1069 "q-65071" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335788 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335788 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${f}_{yxx}(x,y)$ given that $f(x,y)={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335788 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ab0f3803-2840-52ec-8174-767389c2fcc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186335788 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y\\operatorname{l